# component: drawer
# decisions: A11Y-9, DOC-1, DOC-2, OVL-13, OVL-21, LAY-17, OVL-25, BRD-12, LAY-24
# hunks:
#   LAY-24 (operator, 2026-11-19, "go ahead with the robust fix for both mac and windows"): with
#     `data-desktop-titlebar` on `<html>` (the desktop app), a side (x-axis) or top (`up`) drawer
#     starts at `--shell-globalbar-height`, so it never sits under the window's own buttons; a top
#     drawer's viewport is clipped at that row (`clip-path`), so its bleed, snap points and swipe
#     never paint over it, while the backdrop (outside the viewport) still covers the window.
#   BRD-12: corners are roles, not sizes — every radius is `rounded-control|segment|icon|capsule|chip|inline|mark|item|block|card|bubble|overlay|tile` (operator 2026-11-16, amended 2026-11-18);
#     rows with a fill are `rounded-item`, bordered menus `rounded-card border p-1.25` (16 − 1 − 5 = 10), table rows `row-fill`.
#   OVL-25 (operator, 2026-11-13, agent chat ground up §4.1 "no blur behind dialogs"): the backdrop
#     is `bg-black/20`, `dark:bg-black/50`, with upstream's `supports-backdrop-filter:backdrop-blur-xs`
#     removed, so the page behind a modal stays legible and still and dark mode no longer smears.
#   OVL-13: `DrawerPortal` reads `useInternalThemeScope()` and wraps its children in a
#     `display: contents` element carrying that class. The swipe-overshoot bleed falls back to the
#     runtime `var(--popover)`, not upstream's `var(--color-popover)`: the `@theme inline` bridge
#     resolves once on `:root`, so inside a scoped theme it would paint the root theme's surface.
#   A11Y-9: `DrawerContent` mirrors Base UI's `data-base-ui-inert` markers onto native `inert`
#     through `useModalInert`. No new context: upstream's own `DrawerContext` already carries
#     `modal` into `DrawerContent`, so the hook is gated on the value that is already there —
#     which is why `modal={false}` (the Non Modal section) keeps its outside pointer interaction.
#   OVL-21: the popup floats inset by default — `[--drawer-inset:--spacing(2)]`, `rounded-xl`, a full
#     `border` and a transparent bleed. `Drawer` takes `flush` (carried on upstream's own
#     `DrawerContext`, marked `data-flush` on the popup), which restores upstream's per-direction
#     inner-edge rounding and border with the inset at its `0px` default.
#   LAY-17 (MK 2026-10-13, Regent long-names review): the drawer popup sets `wrap-break-word`, so
#     a long unbroken word breaks inside the drawer rather than running past its edge.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: prettier reflow plus the `registry-stamp.mjs` provenance header (DOC-1); no
#               decision of their own.
